# Corvus.Text.Json.SourceGenerator: analyzer diagnostics in the code this generator produces are not reported.
# The package's build targets copy this file into the folder that holds the generator's output paths and pass it to the
# compiler with the project's other analyzer config files. The section covers only this generator's trees; the bulk
# severity key hides analyzer diagnostics there and never applies to compiler diagnostics (nullable warnings, CS1591
# and the like still report). Analyzers still execute on those trees: stopping them needs a per-diagnostic
# severity that only the project's own configuration can restore for its hand-written files.
# Set <CorvusTextJsonSuppressAnalyzerDiagnosticsInGeneratedCode>false</CorvusTextJsonSuppressAnalyzerDiagnosticsInGeneratedCode>
# in the project to leave analyzer diagnostics in generated code reported.
[Corvus.Text.Json.SourceGenerator/**.g.cs]
dotnet_analyzer_diagnostic.severity = none
